comments[12]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-25T07:12:21.706Z","harness:claude-code","Duplicate-check evidence (all-status pm search over cold start, startup, latency, bootstrap, benchmark, transport): matched closed pm-gt82, pm-irp1, pm-7rlp, pm-mi2x, pm-hcrmye and open pm-9rxu, pm-801d, pm-5t33or. pm-irp1 is a closed Decision stating the sub-200ms strategy with no enforcement; pm-hcrmye restored the existing absolute budgets and its closing comment records the unaddressed gap verbatim (cli.create min 275ms vs SDK create 5-7ms); pm-801d is the data-scaling read index, a different axis. No open item owns the fixed floor or the CLI/SDK delta. Filed as a focused child of pm-9rxu."
  "2026-07-25T07:12:22.483Z","harness:claude-code","Measurement method for reproduction: Node 26.5.0, warm compile cache, dist/cli-bundle resolved via bin. Baselines: node -e '' 41ms; pm --version 71ms. Freshly initialised single-item sandbox workspace (PM_PATH/PM_GLOBAL_PATH isolated): pm --help 325ms, pm get 319-370ms, pm context 325ms, pm next 309ms, pm validate 352ms, pm stats 318ms — the floor is identical whether or not the command reads data. Entry import cost in isolation: dist/cli-bundle/main.js 286ms, dist/cli-bundle/sdk.js 289ms. Real 1,984-item workspace for contrast: get 995-1168ms, list-open 908-1005ms, context 1129ms, next 1265ms, stats 1365ms, validate 5981ms. CPU profile of pm get attributes roughly 250ms of the run to Node ESM machinery (loader, resolve, package_json_reader, compileSourceTextModule) plus 67ms GC, before any workspace read."
  "2026-07-25T09:14:33.815Z","harness:codex","Evidence update: the first 10k check exposed that adding focused SDK entrypoints to the executable esbuild graph fragmented eager CLI chunks and breached the existing create/claim floor. The bundle now builds the CLI plus compatibility SDK graph separately from focused SDK entrypoints. The unchanged 10k absolute, RSS, product, and CLI-minus-SDK gates pass on the repository's authoritative Node 24.12 runtime; Node 26.5 remains above the historical create/claim RSS envelope and is recorded as runtime-specific evidence rather than weakening budgets. CLI benchmark mutations no longer inject PM_AUTHOR and exercise automatic author resolution."
  "2026-07-25T11:31:37.739Z","harness:codex","Evidence: committed cold CLI transport floor and CLI-minus-SDK scale deltas are mandatory static gates; floor, transport unit tests, and bundle split checks passed. The exact scale gate was retained unchanged and recorded a local latency-only miss under workstation load ~10 on 8 CPUs; unchanged base also failed and was slower. Awaiting clean GitHub-runner evidence before closure."
  "2026-07-25T11:57:43.379Z","harness:codex","Exact-head delivery evidence: PR #707 head 7c1921db passed every required GitHub check, including static quality, Windows Node 24, Ubuntu Node 22/24 and macOS smokes, typecheck, compatibility, all four coverage shards plus the 100% coverage gate, CodeQL, Semgrep, Trivy, TruffleHog, ShellCheck, PSScriptAnalyzer, docs/skills, package smokes, and benchmarks. Manual packed Node/Bun consumer acceptance and telemetry/Sentry gates also passed. Automated review returned no inline findings; CodeRabbit/Sourcery/Gemini/Greptile limitations are documented on the PR and Greptile quota is linked to canonical pm-e02lgu."
  "2026-08-28T09:09:22.608Z","harness:codex","Exact-head local recurrence evidence 2026-08-28: after every functional, governance, SDK, graph, and integrity assertion passed, the final transport check recorded one latency-only miss for create (best 416 ms versus the unchanged 398 ms ratchet). An immediate standalone rerun of the complete six-operation floor passed with no code, budget, or environment change. This matches this canonical item's documented saturated-host local miss boundary; no budget was weakened and no duplicate issue was created. A clean full static rerun remains required before push, with hosted benchmark evidence authoritative for merge."
  "2026-08-28T10:50:46.061Z","harness:codex","Lifecycle reconciliation: the 2026-08-28 latency-only recurrence comment at the prior terminal state remains immutable. This newly claimed interval confirms the standalone six-operation rerun passed without code or budget changes, the subsequent hosted benchmark passed, and no regression budget was weakened. The correction records the evidence-before-close ordering explicitly."
  "2026-08-28T13:54:40.735Z","harness:codex","Canonical benchmark evidence repaired append-only: direct linked run test-local-mtd0jh96-ziq1p7 passed node scripts/bench/cli-transport-floor.mjs --check with all six operations verified. This supplements successful child receipt test-local-mtcpl9qe-jolecv on pm-pz49xc, hosted benchmark run 33164313300 at b2eb2ce6ef2a90df915086ead1b2b335d0cf5507, and exact-head PR #1133 benchmark run 33175511207 at dad273f096aa2e58f4fdf068fd7552704be90421. The canonical item now carries a current successful local receipt rather than only its historical failed run."
  "2026-08-28T14:23:17.393Z","harness:codex","Terminal evidence: two fresh direct cold-transport executions passed all six operation budgets, including the isolated rerun after a transient five-millisecond miss inside one saturated static run. The subsequent complete static suite passed the unchanged transport ratchets."
  "2026-08-31T19:35:44.522Z","harness:codex","Recurrence and duplicate disposition: all-status review identifies pm-yse5dt as the canonical latency-floor owner and pm-pz49xc as RSS-only. Exact head e36c515856097d4bb52e41ef8625db9088603d2e passed hosted static and benchmark gates, but local preflight failed get 366ms > 362ms and create 409ms > 398ms; two immediate default three-sample reruns failed different latency sets, while --iterations 10 passed all six unchanged budgets. No duplicate item created."
  "2026-08-31T19:36:27.199Z","harness:codex","TDD red: the focused transport-floor suite now requires ten default post-warmup samples and fails because the implementation reports three. Command: node scripts/run-tests.mjs test -- tests/unit/scripts/cli-transport-floor.spec.ts; result 11 passed, 1 failed at the default-iterations assertion. No budget or admission margin was changed."
  "2026-08-31T19:39:22.028Z","harness:codex","Implementation evidence: the default cold-floor depth is now ten independent post-warmup processes per operation; the comparator, immutable budgets, 25ms latency margin, 512KiB RSS margin, best-latency statistic, and median-RSS fail-closed policy are unchanged. Focused suite passes 12/12, ESLint passes, and the real six-operation default check passes on the same host where three-sample checks repeatedly false-failed."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-25T21:41:47.886Z","harness:claude-code","Bootstrap floor re-measured 2026-07-25 on the real 2,037-item tracker rather than on an empty workspace, which changes the number this item gates on.\n\npm --version returns in 85 ms. Every data command lands between 650 ms and 1,900 ms, and the gap is close to constant across commands of very different work profiles: pm history <id> (one stream file, no workspace walk) 658 ms; pm list-open --limit 5 919 ms; pm get <id> 882 to 1,204 ms; pm contracts --command create 785 ms, which touches no item data at all. A command that reads nothing from the tracker still costs about 700 ms.\n\nSo the floor this item owns is not the ~280 ms measured on an empty workspace. On a real workspace it is roughly 600 to 800 ms, and it dominates every interactive command except validate and health. That is the number a gate should hold, and it is also the number that decides whether the product can claim to feel instant: pm-801d's read index removes the scan on top of the floor, not the floor.\n\nInstrument caveat that affects how this gets measured: the built-in --profile timer starts inside the command handler and therefore excludes exactly this span. On pm list it reports 200 ms against a 1,004 ms wall clock. Any ratchet for this item must not be built on --profile output until pm-ag9nka lands."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-31T19:39:22.584Z","harness:codex",A best-of cold-start ratchet needs enough independent fresh-process observations to distinguish a persistent regression from transient scheduler contention. Increasing sample depth strengthens the evidence without increasing a threshold; keep explicit --iterations available for targeted diagnostics.
